From 40f5325bc94e33beb98899fe647e459a211c30fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yongqin Wang <yongqinwang@roblox.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 23:16:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] [Spec Decode][PP] Share the target's input embedding with
 the drafter

Drafters whose checkpoint ships no embed_tokens alias the target's, which
under PP lives on the first stage while the drafter runs on the last.
Sharing was skipped whenever world_size > 1, and nothing reported it: the
load is skipped for a key the checkpoint lacks and load_weights returns
None, which disables the loader's uninitialized-weight check. The drafter
embedded its proposals through uninitialized memory, so only acceptance
suffered. Most EAGLE3 heads are in this class, including
yuhuili/EAGLE3-LLaMA3.1-Instruct-8B; the head the PP tests use happens to
carry its own table, which is why they did not see this.

Instantiate the target's embed_tokens on the last stage for eagle, eagle3,
dflash and dspark so the regular weight loader populates it, and alias it
into the drafter there. The eagle, dflash and dspark loaders now share one
code path, which raises rather than proceeding when a drafter declares an
embedding that nothing will populate.

Signed-off-by: Yongqin Wang <yongqinwang@roblox.com>
